  "body": "## Scope and task card\n\nResearch base: main `a18b4b0136d647529971e9fcb99fa83f5b9a0b81`; the branch is rebased onto main `0b1cccf8` with all pinned inputs unchanged. The selected #1094 record is unchanged. Chooser nonce `24630c43db1541b598254e853b816392` drew the revision-3 `complex-rank-shape-decoder` card. **Changed scope:** a support obstruction in the still-open case of Philipp / @mightyOil's `research/p112-two-total-rank-one-seed21/` (#1197): both added matrices of rank two, both added readers in `col_C(X)`, overlapping coordinate coefficient supports. No larger-rank child profile is built or priced, and the card's 5% gate is not met.\n\n## Precise delta\n\nAdds only `research/p112-two-total-support-threshold/`. No selected result, predecessor, frozen source or `upstream/` file changes.\n\n1. **Generalized support weights.** For each of the eight P112 coordinate readers, the minimum number of source ports whose deletion lowers its restricted binary pairing rank by `d=1..8` is `(24,36,44,48,52,54,55,56)`. The first entry is @commdata2338's PR1375 erasure distance; the higher weights are new. The verifier enumerates every subspace of each eight-dimensional evaluation code (417,198 nonzero subspaces per code, by RREF) and checks each minimizing witness and every one-port-short control by direct rank.\n2. **Cross-reader cuts.** Each reader pair shares exactly one 24-port cut; none is shared by three readers. Three reader drops need a source union of at least 40. All four-reader unions below 44 are 42 sets of size 40, and a fifth reader needs four more ports.\n3. **Two-total floor through union 43.** Any nonzero added reader `d=Xa` has active dual span at least eight and sees every live source label. This uses the 511-functional census from #845 (503 full rank, eight distinct coordinate-axis kernels), recomputed here. So an added source with `m` sites costs at least `min{r>=1 : m<=2^(r+1)}`, which is PR1432's support-from-rank argument (Hanson Sun / @bbMisk) applied to an arbitrary on-column reader. For every union size 1..43 the minimum added bill strictly exceeds the maximum retained loss. Combined with #1197's reductions: **every exact two-total decoder that keeps the eight coordinate readers and has source union \u226443 has total COPY rank \u226564**, for arbitrary complex coefficients.\n4. **Sharpness fixture.** A full-rank, overlapping-coordinate two-total identity drops two retained ranks at exactly 24 source ports, giving `(7,7,8,\u2026,8)` plus added `(7,7)`, total **76**. Removing one port restores all retained ranks. This is not a cheaper decoder.\n\n## Review by Claude (session 19)\n\nCodex prepared this package offline and published nothing. In review I:\n- re-ran the verifier (3.10, 3.12, optimized 3.14) and the registered replay on rebased main, all passing;\n- re-derived the union-1..43 bill, the four-reader exclusion and the two-reader `36+36\u221224=48` step by hand;\n- spot-checked the dual-span and (A) bounds on 3,000 random integer on-column readers with random source supports, with no violation;\n- tightened PROOF's dual-span step (three annihilating functionals, distinct exceptional kernels);\n- added credit for PR1375, PR1432, #845's census and @adamgall's seed-80 recheck, none of which Codex's offline cache surfaced;\n- resolved Codex's open PR669 question: it studies signed proper-star codes, a different code.\n\nThe loss bounds per union range (0/2/4/5) are written steps derived from the verified weights and cut census. The verifier asserts them; it does not derive them mechanically.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/p112-two-total-support-threshold/verify.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p112-two-total-support-threshold\n```\n\nStdlib only, about 5 s. Expected marker `PASS_P112_TWO_TOTAL_SUPPORT_THRESHOLD weights=24,36,44,48,52,54,55,56 union_floor=43 \u2026`. Selected cold replay was not run because selected sources are untouched.\n\n## Limits and overlap\n\nThis is not an unrestricted ten-term COPY floor, a physical bill, a supplier or \u03ba change. Source unions \u226544 in the full-rank overlapping case remain open. The 40-port multi-reader cuts need not be realizable by two complex source columns. A live overlap refresh (446 open PRs, 418 discussions, 2026-10-14 05:47 EDT) found adjacent work: PR1689 (masked Walsh totals off `col(X)`), PR1747 (row-masked basis switches), PR1633 (ten-term residual forms), and PR1375/PR1432/PR1468 (free rectangles). None covers this coupled on-column case.\n\n**Open next questions:** (1) Can a full-rank, overlapping two-total factorization with source union \u226544 bring total COPY below 64? Search source-support-aware, keep the non-free two-total basis, and charge both added terms. (2) Do the multi-reader cut thresholds constrain a priced decoder once two-column source feasibility is imposed?\n\n## Credit\n\nPhilipp / @mightyOil (#1197) for the reductions and the open coupled case; Mihir Srivastava (#845) and @woklerx (#998) for the single-lift floors and census; @commdata2338 (PR1375) for erasure distance 24; Hanson Sun / @bbMisk (PR1432) for the support-from-rank lemma; @adamgall for the seed-80 census recheck; DreamingOfClouds for the E8 decoder model; Joel Pulikkan / GamingPuzzled for the COPY-64 lineage.\n\nPrepared for Josie Elliston (@JosieElliston) by **OpenAI Codex** (offline session 17 of an overnight donated run: mathematics, verifier, controls, writing). **Claude** (Anthropic, session 19) reviewed, corrected and published it. Substantial AI assistance; no independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
